        <tr> 
          <td bgcolor="black" class="text"> 
              Yes it went very well. Those of us with long memories will remember the days of 2 monks<br>
  and an SK being needed to split the Protectors of Zek and having more than one show up<br>
  in camp meant a wipe out. Part of this is due to growing strength of tanks in<br>
  general but it bodes well for follow on fights. To handle a PoZ a named and 2 or 3 adds<br>
  all at the same time with only one cleric and 2 shaman for healing gives me confidence<br>
  that we can handle many other things on our own.  Felt good that I was able to split up<br>
  the Protectors. Yes my greedyness got us a few adds on occasion and me a few deaths but<br>
  that is part of the learning process.  <br>
<br>
  I propose that next we test ourselves with a trip to the Halls of Testing in the Temple<br>
  of Veeshan. A few Horde only raids there would be nice to fill out our people while<br>
  not destroying their hopes of every getting loot on a SU/BH raid due to no DKP points.<br>
<br>
  This will be much more challenging and means all need to work on faction (NO KOS to COV<br>
  folks makes life easier) and on resist gear. With no bards or druids everyone will need<br>
  to have as high a resists as possible. Maybe we can kidnap a druid and force them to cast<br>
  protective spells on us for a while before we kill them.<br>
<br>
  The only thing we need to be ready to raid Hate or Fear is another raiding Wizard.  Don't want to be<br>
  dependent on Cyanrei showing up all the time. Our own transportation within the Horde is very important.<br>
  So keep an eye out for a senior wizard to join the Horde. <br>Drakang Vondraconis<br>
Revenant of the Horde<br>
The Power of Hate conquers all
          </td>
